From bf3841cf540011912f9805bbf0edba297b99a531 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 17:29:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Play a project's coverVideo on hover in the grid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Projects collection already had a coverVideo field — §4 of the
spec calls it out as "loop breve per l'hover in griglia" — but
ProjectCard only ever rendered the still cover; the field sat unused.

Adds ProjectCover, a small client component that stacks the loop on
top of the still cover (which doubles as its poster) inside a new
relative wrapper. It stays at preload="none" with no <source> parked
on the video until the pointer actually enters — nothing ever fetches
for a project without a hover intent — and .play()/.pause() are
called directly rather than left to an autoplay attribute, so the
clip always restarts from frame zero on the next hover. A
`(hover: hover)` check keeps this a mouse-only affordance, matching
the "hover" the spec actually asks for rather than firing on a tap
that's mid-navigation anyway.

Projects without a coverVideo are unaffected: ProjectCover renders
only the existing MediaImage in that case, same markup as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
